Title: Christmas, Facing West
Credit: Teaser trailer, plain-dialogue draft
Draft date: 2026-11-23
Format: Teaser, about 71 seconds
Vocabulary: rph-annotations/1

[[def mus:theme kind=score "Original piano motif, five rising notes. Only four play until the final card."]]

[[def mus:comedy kind=score "Upright bass, brushed snare and celesta; light swing."]]

[[def mus:store-carol kind=diegetic "Tinny holiday tune on a convenience-store speaker. Original or cleared."]]

[[def mus:tannenbaum kind=diegetic "Community brass band playing O Tannenbaum. Record fresh; the composition is public domain."]]

[[def char:JESS look="pretty woman of 28, wavy dark brown hair in a loose messy updo, warm brown eyes, camel wool coat, chunky red knit scarf" "Late 20s. Bright, articulate, slightly breathless. Speeds up when defensive, slows down when honest. Audition A, armored: speed as armor. Audition B, frayed: warm, tired, funny through exhaustion."]]

[[def char:BEN look="handsome man about 30, tousled curly brown hair, stubble, grease-smudged blue denim work shirt with rolled sleeves, shop rag" "About 30. Low-to-mid voice, unhurried, dry. Never pushes a joke; wins by waiting. Audition A, amused: enjoying her. Audition B, guarded: the humor covers a sting."]]

[[def char:LINDA look="woman of 58, short silver-blonde bob, reading glasses on a beaded chain, red cardigan" "Late 50s. Central Pennsylvania warmth, light regional cadence, no caricature. Unflappable, cheerful; delivers bombshells like a weather report and never sounds hurt."]]

[[def char:DOT look="woman in her mid-seventies, weathered face, blaze-orange hunting cap, brown canvas barn coat" "70s. Gravel and deadpan. Appraises; never complains."]]

[[def char:PA-VOLUNTEER "Small-town civic dad, mic too close."]]

# Stage 1: She refuses, then she has to come home

INT. MANHATTAN OFFICE - NIGHT #01#[[at=0:00 dur=9]]

= Jess turns down Christmas; the siren answers for her.

Black.[[id=01a shot=BLACK dur=2]]

Jess at her desk at nine at night. Her window faces a brick airshaft lit by someone else's fluorescent light.[[id=01b shot=MS(JESS) move=push-in/slow img=office-airshaft amb=office-hvac:in,keyboard:in]]

JESS
(still typing, apologizing)
Mom, I'm sorry. I can't come home for Christmas this year. Work is crazy.[[id=01c to=LINDA emo=worried:2,guilty:1 act=placate]]

LINDA
(on the phone; warm, unhurried, a woman who has never once raised her voice to win)
Oh, honey. I understand.[[id=01d to=JESS fx=phone emo=affectionate:2 act=disarm pace=slow]]

A siren rises on Linda's end of the line only.[[id=01e sfx=vehicle.siren-approach fx=phone]]

JESS
(typing stops)
Mom? Is that a siren?[[id=01f emo=worried:2 act=probe pre=0.6 amb=keyboard:out]]

LINDA
(pleasant, as if it's the mailman)
Don't worry, sweetheart. I think it's for me.[[id=01g fx=phone emo=content:2 act=reassure]]

The siren bends down in pitch and becomes a single piano note.[[id=01h bridge=sfx:vehicle.siren-approach>mus:theme mus=theme:in amb=office-hvac:out]]

INT./EXT. JESS'S TESLA, ROUTE 422 - NIGHT #02#[[at=0:09 dur=4]]

= She promises work: two days.

Sleet in the headlights. Jess grips the wheel, still in her office clothes.[[id=02a shot=MCU(JESS) move=push-in/slow img=tesla-422-sleet mus=theme:play]]

Her boss is a faint, impatient murmur over the car speaker.[[id=02b sfx=voice.murmur-indistinct fx=car-speaker]]

JESS
(hiding the panic)
My mom's in the hospital. Two days. I'll be back in two days, I promise.[[id=02c emo=worried:2,confident:1 act=bargain]]

INT./EXT. HOSTETTER HOUSE, ANNVILLE - NIGHT #03#[[at=0:13 dur=7]]

= She comes home. The injury is real, small and funny.

Main Street, lights strung across it.[[id=03a shot=ELS move=pan-right/slow img=annville-main-street]]

>ANNVILLE, PENNSYLVANIA<[[id=03b card=lower-third]]

In the yard, an inflatable snowman lies half-deflated beside a fallen ladder.[[id=03c shot=LS img=yard-snowman-ladder]]

The storm door bangs open and lets snow in. Linda in her recliner, walking boot propped up, surrounded by neighbors' casseroles. Jess in the doorway, coat on, bag in hand.[[id=03d shot=MS(LINDA) img=linda-recliner sfx=door.storm-door-bang amb=tv-low:in]]

LINDA
(lighting up, completely casual)
You came home![[id=03e to=JESS emo=happy:3 act=welcome pace=medium]]

JESS
(breathless, four hours of driving in her voice)
Mom, you were in an ambulance![[id=03f emo=afraid:2,angry:1 act=scold stress=ambulance]]

LINDA
(reasonable)
It's a sprained ankle, sweetheart. They offered.[[id=03g emo=content:2 act=dismiss]]

Jess kneels by the boot. Linda's hand goes to her cheek.[[id=03h shot=TWO(JESS,LINDA,size=MCU) move=hold img=hand-on-cheek mus=theme:play]]

# Stage 2: She tries to leave and gets stuck

EXT. TURKEY HILL - DAWN #04#[[at=0:20 dur=6]]

= She leaves on schedule. The plow stops her.

Sodium lights and slush. Jess's roller bag sits in the Tesla's back seat.[[id=04a shot=LS img=turkey-hill-dawn sfx=door.store-chime mus=theme:stop,store-carol:in note="Keep store signage soft-focus unless cleared."]]

The Tesla backs out with its soft low-speed hum. Jess has a coffee in one hand, her phone at her ear.[[id=04b shot=MS(JESS) img=jess-backing-out sfx=vehicle.ev-pedestrian-hum]]

JESS
(on the phone, brisk, already gone in her head)
She's fine. I'll be back in the office by noon--[[id=04c emo=confident:2 act=assure end=cutoff]]

Crunch. The bumper meets the yellow plow blade of an old pickup. A little ice falls.[[id=04d shot=INSERT(bumper) img=bumper-plow sfx=impact.bumper-plow,debris.ice-fall ovl=0.1]]

One full second of nothing but the store carol.[[id=04e dur=1]]

Dot, seventies, blaze-orange cap, coffee in hand by the door. Unmoved.[[id=04f shot=MS(DOT) img=dot-blaze-cap]]

DOT
(appraising, not angry)
Well, honey. You're not going anywhere today.[[id=04g emo=interested:1 act=appraise pace=slow pre=0.3]]

INT. KREIDER'S AUTO - DAY #05#[[at=0:26 dur=8]]

= The mechanic is her high-school crush. He remembers her; she pretends not to remember him.

An impact wrench rips. One bay, the space heater glowing orange. Ben's boots stick out from under the Tesla.[[id=05a shot=LS img=garage-boots sfx=tool.impact-wrench mus=store-carol:out,comedy:in amb=shop-radio:in,space-heater:in]]

The creeper rolls out.[[id=05b sfx=foley.creeper-roll]]

BEN
(sees her; tiny pause)
Jess Hostetter. Hi.[[id=05c to=JESS emo=interested:2,amused:1 act=greet pace=slow pre=0.4]]

Jess, in a city coat too thin for the weather.[[id=05d shot=MCU(JESS) img=jess-thin-coat]]

JESS
(too bright)
Hi! I'm sorry. Do I know you?[[id=05e emo=embarrassed:3 act=deflect]]

Ben wipes his hands. Not smiling yet.[[id=05f shot=MCU(BEN) img=ben-wiping-hands]]

BEN
(lets it sit a beat; dry)
Ben Kreider. We had chemistry together. You sat right behind me.[[id=05g emo=amused:1 act=needle pre=0.8]]

JESS
(caught)
Ben. Of course. Hi.[[id=05h emo=embarrassed:2 act=concede pace=slow]]

INT. KREIDER'S AUTO / JESS'S CHILDHOOD BEDROOM - DAY #06#[[at=0:34 dur=5]]

= The forced stay.

Ben holds a cracked bumper sensor up to the light.[[id=06a shot=INSERT(sensor) img=cracked-sensor]]

BEN
The sensor's cracked. The part has to come from the factory.[[id=06b emo=content:1 act=inform]]

JESS
(urgent)
How long?[[id=06c emo=worried:3 act=demand]]

BEN
It gets here the twenty-sixth.[[id=06d emo=content:1 act=inform]]

JESS
Of December? That's after Christmas![[id=06e emo=incredulous:3 act=plead stress=December]]

BEN
(beat, gently)
Looks like you're home for Christmas.[[id=06f emo=amused:1,affectionate:1 act=console pace=slow pre=0.8]]

The roller bag back on Jess's childhood bed, under a high-school pennant.[[id=06g shot=MS img=bag-on-bed mus=comedy:resolve]]

INT. KREIDER'S AUTO - DAYS LATER (SERIES OF SHOTS) #07#[[at=0:39 dur=3]]

= Days pass. She still asks, out of habit.

The same garage doorway three times. Her coat changes, the snow deepens, one coffee becomes two.[[id=07a shot=MS(JESS) img=doorway-1,doorway-2,doorway-3 mus=comedy:sting note="One celesta note per still."]]

JESS
(leaning in the doorway, by rote)
Any news on the part?[[id=07b emo=bored:2 act=check]]

BEN
(doesn't look up)
Not yet.[[id=07c emo=content:1 act=dismiss]]

# Stage 3: She chooses to stay

EXT. FARM LANE, EDGE OF TOWN - SUNSET #08#[[at=0:42 dur=9]]

= The turn. Work calls; she lets it go.

Ben's truck faces a wide field and the low sun. Two silhouettes, a bench seat of space between them.[[id=08a shot=TWO(BEN,JESS,size=MS) move=push-in/slow img=truck-rear-window mus=theme:drop amb=truck-idle:in,heater-fan:in,crows-distant:in note="Music drops to one held string note."]]

Jess in profile, lit orange. A few flakes drift.[[id=08b shot=CU(JESS) move=push-in/slow img=jess-profile-sunset]]

JESS
(quiet but voiced, not whispered; half a laugh at herself)
In the city, I never get to see the sun go down. It's just gone by four o'clock.[[id=08c to=BEN emo=wistful:2,amused:1 act=confide vol=soft pace=slow]]

Her phone lights up on the dash: WORK. It buzzes. Her hand turns it face-down. The buzzing stops.[[id=08d shot=INSERT(phone) img=phone-tyler sfx=phone.vibrate-dash pre=1.5]]

Ben turns the key. The engine stops. Wind, and the engine block ticking.[[id=08e sfx=vehicle.engine-off,vehicle.engine-tick amb=truck-idle:out,heater-fan:out,wind-field:in]]

BEN
(low, simple)
Stay a while. It's worth the wait.[[id=08f to=JESS emo=affectionate:2 act=invite vol=soft pace=slow pre=1.0]]

The theme returns, four notes. The fifth is held back.[[id=08g mus=theme:play]]

INT. KREIDER'S AUTO, OFFICE - DAY #09#[[at=0:51 dur=5]]

= The overheard remark. It hurts because she was starting to stay.

Jess in the office doorway with a cardboard tray of two coffees.[[id=09a shot=MS(JESS) img=jess-coffee-tray mus=theme:stop amb=space-heater:in]]

BEN (O.S.)
(to his uncle, matter-of-fact)
Don't get attached. She'll be gone the minute that car is fixed.[[id=09b to=UNCLE emo=content:1 act=assess]]

The cardboard tray crunches in her hand.[[id=09c shot=CU(JESS) img=jess-tray-crunch sfx=foley.cardboard-crunch]]

JESS
(very level)
Is that really what you think of me?[[id=09d emo=hurt:2,angry:2 act=challenge pace=slow]]

Ben turns around, caught.[[id=09e shot=MCU(BEN) img=ben-caught]]

BEN
(half a second too late)
Jess, wait. That's not what I meant.[[id=09f emo=embarrassed:2 act=backpedal pre=0.5]]

EXT. ANNVILLE TOWN SQUARE - NIGHT #10#[[at=0:56 dur=4]]

= The convention, promised and withheld.

Crowd, breath steam, kids on shoulders. The tree is still dark.[[id=10a shot=ELS img=square-crowd mus=tannenbaum:in amb=crowd-murmur:in]]

Jess alone in the crowd, scanning.[[id=10b shot=MS(JESS) img=jess-in-crowd]]

Ben's truck parked at the edge of the square, empty.[[id=10c shot=LS img=truck-empty]]

PA VOLUNTEER
(mic too close, civic cheer)
Okay, folks! Let's light this tree![[id=10d fx=pa emo=excited:2 act=rally vol=loud]]

CROWD
Five! Four! Three! Two--[[id=10e emo=excited:3 vol=x-loud pace=medium end=cutoff mus=tannenbaum:out,theme:swell]]

SMASH CUT TO:[[cut=hard]]

.BLACK #11#[[at=1:00 dur=1]]

Total silence, longer than is comfortable.[[id=11a shot=BLACK dur=1 mus=theme:stop amb=crowd-murmur:out]]

.TITLE #12#[[at=1:01 dur=3]]

A field at the last edge of sunset, the horizon low in the frame.[[id=12a shot=ELS move=hold img=field-last-light mus=theme:hold note="One piano chord on the theme's fourth note, held."]]

>CHRISTMAS, FACING WEST<[[id=12b card=title]]

INT. HOSTETTER HOUSE - NIGHT #13#[[at=1:04 dur=4]]

= The button: the car has been ready for days, and she still hasn't left.

Linda in the recliner, the landline cord around one finger, eating pie straight from the tin.[[id=13a shot=MS(LINDA) img=linda-pie-phone]]

LINDA
(low, conspiratorial, delighted)
Dot, her car's been ready since Tuesday.[[id=13b to=DOT emo=mischievous:2 act=confide vol=soft pace=medium]]
(beat)
And she still hasn't left.[[id=13c to=DOT emo=mischievous:3,pleased:2 act=reveal vol=soft pace=slow pre=0.6]]

.LIGHTS #14#[[at=1:08 dur=3.5]]

= The lighting we were denied, and the theme's fifth note.

The heavy clunk of the tree lights switching on. The crowd goes "Ohhh!" and cheers. Sleigh bells.[[id=14a shot=BLACK dur=0.6 sfx=electric.relay-clunk,crowd.cheer-ooh,bells.sleigh mus=theme:resolve]]

Black blooms into warm, out-of-focus tree lights. We never see the tree or the couple.[[id=14b shot=ECU(lights) move=pull-out/slow img=tree-bokeh]]

>COMING THIS CHRISTMAS<[[id=14c card=title]]

/*
PRODUCTION NOTES

Dialogue rule: every line must make sense heard once, out of context, over a phone speaker. Complete sentences, no inside references, no trailing half-lines. Medium pace unless a line says otherwise.

Picture rule: never show a face in close-up while that character is speaking. Play the line over the listener, an object or a silhouette.

Look: warm, saturated Christmas-movie stills. Jess always in the camel coat and red scarf; Ben in the denim work shirt with a shop rag.

On-screen text: three cards only. ANNVILLE, PENNSYLVANIA; the title; COMING THIS CHRISTMAS.

Payoffs to protect when cutting:
- "I can't come home for Christmas" in the first line pays off in "Looks like you're home for Christmas" and the final card.
- "Two days" and "back by noon" set up "Of December?"
- "Any news on the part?" "Not yet." sets up "her car's been ready since Tuesday."
- The fifth note of the theme is held back until the last card.

Withheld: whether she stays in Annville; the reconciliation; any kiss or touch between Jess and Ben.

Voices: record every line on its own track. Build pauses and overlaps in the edit, not in the voice model.
*/
